Fork PR (same branch, for browsing): https://github.com/AlexPerrin/OpenRune-Server/pull/10

Content area from OpenRune/OpenRune-Server#353 (answers there: all of it, one PR per row, ids renumbered against main, wiki data is fine).

From our per-feature patch `16-genie-random-event` (in [`openrune/upstream/`](https://github.com/AlexPerrin/osrs-plugins-reverse/tree/main/openrune/upstream) of osrs-plugins-reverse), on `main` (`c2492318d`).

**Problem.** There were no random events.

**Change.** New module `content/events/random-events` with the Genie, scheduled by the OSRS Wiki's random event spawn mechanics ("Random events", section "Spawn mechanics", which quotes Mod Ash for each rule):
- **When.** The next event is due 1-2 hours after the last one, on a real-time clock that keeps running while the player is logged out. The due time is stored in a persistent player attribute (`random_event_next_at`, epoch milliseconds), so it survives logout and restarts. A soft timer checks every 5 minutes of play (500 ticks) whether it is due.
- **Offline.** If the event came due while the player was offline, the due time moves forward by 10-70 minutes on login, as many times as needed to land in the future, and keeps counting.
- **Where not.** When it is due and the player is somewhere random events are not allowed, the event is missed and a new 1-2 hours is rolled. The places covered: inside a bank with a bank booth (a booth within 7 tiles) or in front of a bank chest (within 2 tiles), except Ferox Enclave; the Grand Exchange's stone square; the God Wars Dungeon, Ancient Cavern, Waterbirth Island Dungeon, Ruins of Tapoyauik and Charred Dungeon (cache areas); and instances (boss lairs and minigames run in instances here).
- **Transformed.** No event while the player's model is altered (transformation ring, greegree): it is missed in the same way. A Genie that is already out leaves at once if the player transforms (Mod Ash: "the genie would delete itself when it realised you'd equipped that").
- **Busy.** An open interface or a Make-X repeat (a pending weak queue, which is how Make-X loops run here) holds a due event back. It is retried every tick and spawns as soon as the player is free.
- **One at a time.** No second event NPC while the Genie is out.
- **The Genie** (unchanged from the first version of this PR): appears beside the player, faces them and says "Greetings, Master/Mistress <name>!". Every 12 seconds he follows them, banks included (wiki, 1 November 2023), and calls them by name with one of the three transcript lines. Talk-to gives the lamp with the transcript's line. Dismiss sends him away. He leaves after a minute with "Maybe later." when ignored. Another player's Talk-to gets "Sorry, I'm trying to talk to someone else, but he/she seems to be ignoring me." (the owner's pronoun).
- **The lamp:** Rub gives 10 x the chosen skill's level in XP. With a full inventory it is dropped at the player's feet for 3 hours (wiki trivia, Mod Ash: rewards are dropped and stay up to three hours).
- `::randomevent` summons him (like `::star`), bypassing the schedule.

Server-only ids, numbered after the ids already on main and not shared with any of our other PRs, so they merge in any order: timers `random_event` 433 (the 5-minute check), `random_event_genie` 434 (the Genie's calls).

**Tests.** `GenieRandomEventTest` (10, integration):
- spawn beside and facing the owner;
- leaving after a minute;
- the due time is 1-2 h ahead, persisted, and a relog does not restart it;
- an event due while offline moves 10-70 min forward;
- a due event spawns him and rolls the next one;
- in a bank (booth 2 tiles away) it is missed and re-rolled;
- transformed: missed, and a Genie already out leaves;
- an open interface delays it until closed;
- a Make-X weak queue delays it;
- no second NPC while he is out.

How to check in game (each claim above):
1. `::randomevent` shows the Genie beside you, facing you, with the greeting overhead. Walk away: within 12 s he is beside you again with a call line. Ignore him for a minute: "Maybe later." and he is gone.
2. Talk-to gives the lamp. With a full inventory the lamp appears on the floor under you.
3. Rub: choose a skill, gain 10 x its level in XP.
4. Scheduling: the attribute `random_event_next_at` is in the character's saved attributes after a login. The rest is too slow to wait for in game (1-2 h); the tests cover it.

On this branch (Docker `eclipse-temurin:21`, upstream's `./gradlew`, 4 GB container; a clean `freshCache` of main restored first, then `:or-cache:buildCache :or-cache:mergePluginGamevals`, then each task as a separate run, then `run` to "Server ready"): RESULTS_PENDING. `tools/scripts/fix_gameval_conflicts.py --check` finds no conflicts on this branch.

Nothing was checked in game from this exact branch.

**Data sources.** OSRS Wiki (by the wiki's contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/): "Random events" (Spawn mechanics, Locations without random events, Bank locations with random events, Changes, Trivia), "Genie" (incl. Changes), "Transcript:Genie", "Lamp". The spawn rules on the wiki cite Mod Ash's posts, archived on the wiki.

**Caveats.**
- Approximated: the official no-event zones are hand-drawn and not published. Banks are found from bank booths and chests nearby (radii 7 and 2 are ours), the Grand Exchange square is a 27 x 27 box around the wiki's map centre, and instances stand in for "most bosses and minigames". Not covered: the wiki's other entries (Forestry events, Camdozaal golem workshop, Lake Molch, Shayzien Agility Course, Death's Office, Goblin Cave, Stranglewood, The Scar, POH building mode, boats, PvP worlds, Wintertodt prison, the listed minigames that are not instances here), and the per-event restrictions (underwater, Kalphite Lair, Hunter areas). None of these matter for the Genie alone except as places where he can still appear.
- Guesses: missing the event while transformed (the wiki only says it "will not spawn"), and re-rolling 1-2 h when an event comes due while the Genie is still out. Treating any pending weak queue as a Make-X repeat. The 1-tick retry while busy (the wiki: it turns up "soon after" the menu closes). The 5-minute check counts from login.
- Unsourced: the lamp uses the base (unboosted) level. The wiki says "level" (Lamp) and "current level" (Genie), and neither says whether boosts count. "Your wish has been granted!" on Rub, and no chat message when the lamp is given (since 9 September 2021 the game says what you received, but the wording is not on the wiki). "He isn't interested in you." on another player's Dismiss.
- Not implemented: the transcript's "Have a nice day, Master/Mistress." when talked to in a zone without random events (the Genie still gives the lamp there); the underwater Genie; the lamp's skill restrictions (members' skills on free worlds, Construction without a house, Runecraft/Herblore/Sailing before their quests), which belong to the shared lamp chooser. Other random events could build on the same schedule.

**Release note.** The Genie random event, on OSRS's random event schedule.

